# >>> fleet envclass ignore (kanban t_8922e052) - do not duplicate <<<
# Secrets never enter the tree. Real values live in /etc/swift/env/funnelswift.env. The patterns below cover the
# CLASS that fleet/tracked-secret-check.sh refuses to publish (.env / .env.<anything>,
# .pem/.key/.p12/.pfx/.keystore/.jks, id_rsa id_ed25519 id_ecdsa .npmrc .netrc .pgpass
# credentials.json), so no lane can `git add` a path that would then refuse every push from
# this repo. Written as character classes because the gate lowercases every basename and git
# does not: a plain `*.pem` rule still lets SERVER.PEM be committed first. The three
# negations are exactly the gate's TEMPLATE allowlist (.example/.sample/.template) and must
# stay LAST, or .env.example stops being committable and the documented fix for this class
# becomes impossible in this repo.
.[eE][nN][vV]
.[eE][nN][vV].*
*.[pP][eE][mM]
*.[kK][eE][yY]
*.[pP]12
*.[pP][fF][xX]
*.[kK][eE][yY][sS][tT][oO][rR][eE]
*.[jJ][kK][sS]
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
.npmrc
.netrc
.pgpass
credentials.json
!*.example
!*.sample
!*.template

# THE MAIL CLIENT IS TRACKED SOURCE (kanban t_5ef8ffc6). The bare build-artifact pattern above
# (funnelswift) matches ANY path component named funnelswift, which swallowed www-mail/funnelswift/ whole: 13
# served files sat on disk, ignored by git, so a clone of this repo had no mail client at all and the
# front-end push gate could not judge them (it skips a file the app repo does not track). Re-include
# the directory and everything in it; the artifact ignore above still applies to build outputs.
!www-mail/funnelswift/
!www-mail/funnelswift/**
